Subject: [PATCH 32/33] =?UTF-8?q?perf:=20GGML=5FCUDA=5FFA=5FVEC=5FGQA=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20FlashAttention=20vec=20kernel=20walks=20each=20K/V?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20head=20once=20for=20its=208=20query=20heads=20(quantized=20K?=
 =?UTF-8?q?V=20decode)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With grouped-query attention (Qwen3.6: 16 query heads on 2 K/V heads) the vec kernel launched one block per query head, so
every K/V row was walked and dequantized 8x per decode step. The kernel gets a second column dimension ncols2 = query heads
of one K/V head: a block now owns a head group, shares the K walk and dequantizes each V row once for all of them.

Dispatch: head size 256, gqa_ratio % 8 == 0, no ALiBi / softcap, K/V q4_0, q8_0 or q8_0/q5_1. F16 K/V only with
GGML_CUDA_FA_VEC_GQA_F16=1 (unmeasured; upstream sends F16 to the MMA / tile kernels).
GGML_CUDA_FA_VEC_GQA: 0 = off, 1 (default) = single-token decode, 2 = also 2-4 token verify batches (slower, but needs no F16
KV copy: ~7 MiB compute buffer instead of ~700 MiB at 262k).

fa1: decode from a 131k q4_0 slot 12.68 -> 13.99 t/s (+10.3%) with a byte-identical reply; test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_EXT
4079/4079 under modes 0, 1, 2 and F16; new cases: hs 256, gqa 8/16, q4_0 / q8_0 / q8_0+q5_1 / f16, 1-5 tokens, sinks.
